Phase 1: In-Database ML, Systems, and Data-Centric AI Pioneers
These experts focus on executing machine learning directly inside the database engine, minimizing data movement and maximizing throughput—vital for enterprise products.

Dr. Samuel Madden (USA – MIT)
Focus: Database systems, distributed data processing, and machine learning integration. Known for core research on how data management systems can natively support machine learning models and analytics.
Dr. Tim Kraska (Switzerland / USA – MIT)
Focus: Learned index structures and machine learning for systems. He pioneered the concept of replacing traditional B-Trees and database indexes with machine learning models to drastically speed up data retrieval.
Dr. Stratos Idreos (Greece / USA – Harvard University)
Focus: Data systems architecture, adaptive database design, and automated physical database design. Highly relevant for building self-optimizing database products.
Dr. Azza Abouzied (Egypt / UAE – NYU Abu Dhabi)
Focus: Human-in-the-loop data analytics, database interfaces, and visual data exploration tools. Useful for designing intuitive user interfaces for database administrators and ML workflows.
Dr. Jignesh M. Patel (India / USA – University of Wisconsin-Madison)
Focus: Enterprise database architectures, query optimization, and hardware-accelerated data processing (leveraging modern CPU/GPU caches for database workloads).

Phase 2: Graph, Vector, and Large-Scale Enterprise Data Architects
Crucial if your product leverages Oracle AI Vector Search, graph data management, or large language model (LLM) embeddings mapped against relational data structures.
Dr. Alon Halevy (Israel / USA – Meta / Ex-Google / University of Washington)
Focus: Data integration, data lakes, structured data management, and semantic web technologies. Essential reference for unifying unstructured and structured data schemas.
Dr. Divesh Srivastava (India / USA – AT&T Research)
Focus: Data quality, data integration, and graph data management. His work helps build fault-tolerant data pipelines that maintain high integrity under heavy enterprise loads.
Dr. Gerhard Weikum (Germany – Max Planck Institute for Informatics)
Focus: Autonomous database tuning, knowledge graphs, and scalable text/data mining. A titan in European database research with deep insights into automated system health tracking.
Dr. Minos Garofalakis (Greece – Technical University of Crete)
Focus: Data streams, approximate query processing, and machine learning synchronization over massive relational datasets.
Dr. Josee Tremblay (Canada – École Polytechnique de Montréal)
Focus: Enterprise systems integration, high-performance computing, and resilient corporate data architectures.

Phase 3: Automated Machine Learning (AutoML) & Scalable Optimization
Valuable for engineering background monitoring tools, automated alert analysis, and predictive index optimization.
Dr. Amol Deshpande (India / USA – University of Maryland)
Focus: Probabilistic databases, cloud-native data systems, and query optimization for complex, uncertain enterprise data workloads.
Dr. Feifei Li (China / USA – Alibaba / University of Utah)
Focus: Cloud databases, distributed data systems, and AI-driven autonomous database infrastructure operations. Highly relevant for cloud-scale architectures (like OCI environments).
Dr. Nesime Tatbul (Turkey / USA – Intel Labs / MIT)
Focus: Time-series analytics, stream processing, and real-time anomaly detection—foundational for real-time alert monitors and log diagnostics.
Dr. Xuemin Lin (China / Australia – University of New South Wales)
Focus: Graph databases, spatial-temporal data management, and large-scale data mining algorithms.
Dr. Bettina Kemme (Germany / Canada – McGill University)
Focus: Distributed database replication, high availability, consistency protocols, and database recovery systems.

Phase 4: Applied AI Engineering & Enterprise Systems Integration
Focusing on the practical application layer, translating raw machine learning inference into clean, low-latency enterprise operations.
Dr. Matei Zaharia (Romania / USA – Stanford University / Databricks)
Focus: Large-scale data processing architectures, unified analytics, and integrating machine learning lifecycles with enterprise data platforms.
Dr. Raghu Ramakrishnan (India / USA – Microsoft / University of Wisconsin)
Focus: Database systems, data mining, and massive-scale cloud data architecture. A legendary figure in combining database logic with advanced data science.
Dr. Timos Sellis (Greece / Australia – Swinburne University of Technology)
Focus: Spatial databases, data warehousing, and advanced indexing structures.
Dr. Shan Lu (China / USA – University of Chicago)
Focus: Software reliability, bug-finding automation, and performance diagnostics in complex multi-tier database and software infrastructures.
Dr. Magdalena Balazinska (Poland / USA – University of Washington)
